      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T20:05:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we make it, like this?\n```\n\tif (rc \u003d\u003d EC_RES_BUSY)\n\t\treturn EC_RES_BUSY;\n\n\tif (rc \u003d\u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS) {\n\t\tr-\u003eflags \u003d crec_flash_get_protect();\n\n\t\t/* Indicate which flags are valid on this platform */\n\t\tr-\u003evalid_flags \u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_GPIO_ASSERTED |\n\t\t\t\t EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_STUCK |\n\t\t\t\t EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_INCONSISTENT |\n\t\t\t\t EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_UNKNOWN |\n\t\t\t\t crec_flash_physical_get_valid_flags();\n\t\tr-\u003ewritable_flags \u003d\n\t\t\tcrec_flash_physical_get_writable_flags(r-\u003eflags);\n\n\t\targs-\u003eresponse_size \u003d sizeof(*r);\n        } else {\n\t        /* Clear error and wait for the next request. */\n\t        flash_protect_async_data.rc \u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS;\n        }\n\tbreak;\n```\n\nCurrently, `flash_protect_async_data.rc \u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS` doesn\u0027t make sense here because we reset return code to EC_RES_SUCCESS only when....rc is already EC_RES_SUCCESS.\n\nOne note here. If the caller sends `FLASH_PROTECT_GET_RESULT` without previous `FLASH_PROTECT_ASYNC` then it just returns the current status. For me, it\u0027s feature rather than a bug 😄",
